        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: निमित्तम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निमित्तम् — nimittam — \"an occasion; a cause\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विवाहः मम आगमनस्य निमित्तम् अस्ति। vivāhaḥ mama āgamanasya nimittam asti. A wedding is the occasion of my visit."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निमित्तम् (nimittam) MW gives nimitta the senses \"a mark\", \"a sign\" and \"a cause, a motive, a ground\", and says it is possibly connected with ni and the root √mā, \"to measure\"; so its origin is uncertain (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
